      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>An original Aramaic-language “meturgeman piyyuṭ” for Simḥat Torah. I’m working on creating a seder meturgeman liturgy, akin to those for day 7 of Pesaḥ and for Shavuot, to be recited on Simḥat Torah. Mostly incorporating older Aramaic poems, I’ve also decided to write some originals myself. This piyyuṭ, written in the structure of the famous Aqdamut Milin reshut still recited on Shavuot, is meant to be inserted before the translation of the first verse of the first aliyah on Simḥat Torah. It discusses the halakhic status and history of Shmini Atseret, as well as the final blessing and death of Moses.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
